     Welcome to the world of soldier ants and orcs armed with poison
arrows.  You've passed the point you can expect to see monsters who
get generated in small groups instead of as single critters, so the
increase is real.  Monsters appropriate for your level are likely
to start with offensive wands by then (the proverbial kobold with
zapping a wand of death earlier on could only get such a thing by
picking it up off the floor before you did).  Also you've reached
the depth where polymorph traps start occuring; weak monsters like
to use those to try to become strong ones.  Likewise shapechanging
chameleons will be present by then.  Even though those don't use
any particular intelligence to attempt to become nastier foes, the
random forms taken only need to pick a really tough monster once to
pose a substantial threat.


